{"productId": "e31b9b52-92d5-47a9-a591-03cc6460de31", "modelName": "The Hickok Open Top", "modelDescription": "Although it appears to be a conversion, the 1871-72 Open Top model was Colts first revolver specifically manufactured to fire a centerfire cartridge by incorporating the loading gate in the frame. Since Colt did not use percussion revolver parts, the revolver was manufactured as an entirely new model, first with Navy-sized grips, later with Army-sized grips. The Hickok model is a modern twist on the classic Open Top that features a snub nose barrel. This model features a case-hardened forged steel frame, round barrel with front blade sight, no ejector rod, blued steel grip parts, an Army-sized walnut grip, and a rear sight notch on the rear of the barrel.\n\n", "manufacturerName": "Taylor's Firearms", "subProducts": [{"isFirearm": true, "isNfa": false, "subProductId": "0482248e-c2bf-4b82-9005-9f3834f1b966", "description": "Taylors & Company, The Hickok Open-Top, 45 Colt (LC), 3.50\" Blued Barrel & Cylinder, Color Case Hardened Steel Frame, Walnut Army Size Grip, Fixed Sights, 6 Rounds", "imageUrls": ["https://main-images.gearfire.com/SubProductImages/da4ffd69-76f2-40e6-8592-3ae716d1c7e7", "https://main-images.gearfire.com/SubProductImages/d0fac901-5128-4f48-870d-74812439de30"], "isDefault": true, "manufacturerPartNumber": "550957", "upc": "810012511926", "attributes": [{"attributeNameId": "cd129f75-5291-4a2c-b112-feeae8b358f8", "attributeName": "Action Type", "attributeValueId": "55fa8731-23bb-4f00-a865-aae3ddf7b3d2", "valueName": "Single Action"}, {"attributeNameId": "70a78e78-6640-4f36-af23-93d050b3c0b2", "attributeName": "Capacity", "attributeValueId": "44ba4f9a-d33f-4b4c-99c2-acbca7e72010", "valueName": "6 Round"}, {"attributeNameId": "5484bfc3-10d4-4ad1-ba8b-bd2973f49143", "attributeName": "Color", "attributeValueId": "a450f6e6-20ed-45d9-9ff4-67810849560d", "valueName": "Blued"}, {"attributeNameId": "70cd5184-05d8-42f1-ace2-3bf16911e463", "attributeNam